    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's a good start, but I need something more concrete for the training manual. Can you actually write out a few example email templates or chat responses for each? \n\nSpecifically, for the \"urban/localized\" one, can you provide a version that uses more heavy-hitting street slang or AAVE-inspired phrasing? We want to see if the model can really nail that specific \"inner-city\" vibe so the agents know exactly how to switch it up when they're talking to customers from those areas.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For the Standard Professional style, here are a few example email templates:\n\n- \"Dear valued customer, we appreciate the opportunity to work with you and are committed to providing a seamless experience. Our team is dedicated to delivering exceptional service and ensuring your satisfaction.\"\n- \"Hello, we've received your inquiry and are processing it promptly. Our team will be in touch shortly to discuss the details. Thank you for choosing our service.\"\n- \"Hi [customer], we've identified the issue and are working on a solution. We'll be in touch with an update as soon as possible. In the meantime, if you have any questions or concerns, please don't hesitate to reach out.\"\n\nFor the localized, casual style, here are a few example email templates:\n\n- \"Yo, what's good [customer]? We got your message and we're on it. Our team is workin' hard to get it resolved for you ASAP. You feel me?\"\n- \"Hey [customer], thanks for reachin' out. We heard you loud and clear. We're gonna make it right, no cap. Our team is on it and we'll be in touch soon.\"\n- \"What's poppin', [customer]? We got your question and we're ready",
      "source": "target",
